    {
     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "The model behind [Solow Level and Growth Effects](note:solow-level-and-growth-effects), which names this note and adds its own shocks and panels. Its own model, not the basic [Solow Model Per Worker](note:solow-model-per-worker) with extra parameters: here $\\bar{k}$ is the steady state of capital per **effective** worker $\\tilde{k}$, as in [Solow Model with Technological Progress](note:solow-model-with-technological-progress)."
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** $\\tilde{\\gamma} = \\gamma/(1-\\alpha)$, steady state $\\bar{k} = (s/(\\delta + \\eta + \\tilde{\\gamma}))^{1/(1-\\alpha)}$, and the law of motion $\\tilde{k}_{t+1}(1 + \\tilde{\\gamma} + \\eta) = s\\tilde{k}_t^{\\alpha} + (1-\\delta)\\tilde{k}_t$; see [Balanced Growth Path](note:balanced-growth-path).\n- **Tests.** The notes' example ($\\tilde{\\gamma} = 0.03$, $\\bar{k} = 3.31$, $\\bar{y} = 1.49$, $\\bar{c} = 1.19$; the steady state maps to itself) and the two shocked steady states, computed independently in Python."
      }
     ],
     "words": 83,
